<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Monet / dynamic — hands colour back to the wallpaper.

    Intentionally almost empty. Android's Monet engine generates system_accent* and
    system_neutral* at runtime from the wallpaper, and it does that by *applying an
    overlay of its own*. Declaring those resources here would fight it — whichever
    overlay wins is decided by priority, so a fixed value here would either be
    ignored or would silently break dynamic colour. The only thing this theme does
    is leave the generated palette alone.

    A theme with no overrides is not dead weight: it is the "restore defaults"
    option in the switcher, and it is the escape hatch if a fixed palette ever
    renders unreadable against a particular app.
-->
<resources>
    <!-- Nothing else on purpose. See the comment above. -->
</resources>
